## 3.2 GCMC and DFT simulation
To evaluate our ligand functionalization strategy for selective adsorption of ${\mathrm{C}}_{2}{\mathrm{H}}_{6}$ from $\mathrm{C_{2}H_{6}/C_{2}H_{4}}$ mixtures and to further examine the co-adsorption of mixtures on this series of MOFs, the GCMC simulations were carried out for Mn-PNMI. As shown in Figure 4, equimolar mixture was introduced to the structure at $298\mathrm{~K~}$ and 1 bar. After reaching the equilibrium, the ${\mathrm{C}}_{2}{\mathrm{H}}_{6}$ and $\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}$ molecules distributed evenly in the pore channels of Mn-PNMI, and ${\mathrm{C}}_{2}{\mathrm{H}}_{6}$ displayed noticeably higher distribution proportion.
Subsequently, the DFT calculations were conducted according to the GCMC simulation results, introducing ${\mathrm{C}}_{2}{\mathrm{H}}_{6}$ or $\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}$ into the potential location in the framework. The results indicated that rich pyridyl-N atoms and imide-O atoms on the pore surfaces provided very effective ${\mathrm{C}}_{2}{\mathrm{H}}_{6}$ binding sites. Moreover, the relatively short N··· O distance suggested a stronger interaction of ${\mathrm{C}}_{2}{\mathrm{H}}_{6}$ with the structure, which was in good agreement with the adsorption behaviors found experimentally.
